// Title: Outbound Network Connection To Public IP Via Winlogon
// Sigma ID: 7610a4ea-c06d-495f-a2ac-0a696abcfd3b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Christopher Peacock @securepeacock, SCYTHE @scythe_io
// Date: 2023-04-28 | Modified: 2024-03-12
// ATT&CK: execution, command-and-control, stealth, T1218.011
// Description: Detects a "winlogon.exe" process that initiate network communications with public IP addresses
// False positives:
//   - Communication to other corporate systems that use IP addresses from public address spaces
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2023/04/11/guidance-for-investigating-attacks-using-cve-2022-21894-the-blacklotus-campaign/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_winlogon_net_connections.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\winlogon.exe" and (not((ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "127.0.0.0/8") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "10.0.0.0/8") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "172.16.0.0/12") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "192.168.0.0/16") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "169.254.0.0/16") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "::1/128") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "fe80::/10") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "fc00::/7"))))
